│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ rewrite_rowwise_lcp_trie_reorder                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The existing program was broken in many ways: `column_recursion` wrote rows via           │
│                          │ `result_df.loc = ...` into an empty DataFrame (misaligned/mislabeled results), reordered  │
│                          │ *cell values* rather than per-row column permutations (violating the API which must       │
│                          │ return per-row column orderings), dropped the returned `column_orderings` (always `[]`),  │
│                          │ contained column-name mutation bugs, and used adjacency/squared-length heuristics that    │
│                          │ don't match the actual character-Trie prefix objective.                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I rewrote the editable algorithm to directly target the real objective:                   │
│                          │ - Serialize each cell once (empty string for NaN) and factorize values to integer codes.  │
│                          │ - Build up to three bounded whole-dataset candidate per-row column orderings:             │
│                          │   1) A global frequency ordering ranked by `sum(len(v)*count(v)*(count(v)-1))` per column │
│                          │ with deterministic tie breaks;                                                            │
│                          │   2) A recursive conditional prefix partition tree on integer codes, splitting groups on  │
│                          │ the field with the best length-weighted repetition, tail-ordered deterministically;       │
│                          │   3) A variant with a different length/frequency tradeoff.                                │
│                          │ - Score each candidate exactly with the ideal Trie objective: sum of adjacent LCPs after  │
│                          │ sorting the serialized row strings (binary-search LCP with C-speed slice comparisons).    │
│                          │ - Return the best candidate's DataFrame (object dtype, identical values) plus valid       │
│                          │ per-row column orderings (list of column names per row), preserving shape, row identity,  │
│                          │ all cell values, and honoring `col_merge`/`one_way_dep`/stops. Runtime is bounded via     │
│                          │ depth caps, candidate column limits, and shared precomputation.                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0102                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/z-ai/glm-5.3                                                                   │
