│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ serial_trie_candidate_selection_rewrite                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The previous program failed validation for multiple structural reasons: (1) it returned   │
│                          │ an empty `column_orderings` list `[]`, giving the evaluator no valid per-row column       │
│                          │ orderings; (2) `column_recursion` inserted rows via `result_df.loc` from `as_completed`   │
│                          │ futures, scrambling row order and writing into an empty DataFrame with no rows; (3) the   │
│                          │ recursive path mutated/dropped columns (`original_index` handling, group `.iloc` writes)  │
│                          │ and its final shape/value assertions could not hold, so rows and cells were effectively   │
│                          │ lost or altered; (4) `find_max_group_value` mixed pandas/Counter hashing with `getattr`   │
│                          │ attribute lookups on named tuples that don't match real column names. In short, the       │
│                          │ algorithm did not preserve data or produce consistent per-row permutations.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fix replaces the whole editable block with a correct, bounded construction-selection  │
│                          │ algorithm aligned with the true objective (character-Trie reuse measured by sorted-string │
│                          │ adjacent LCP sums): serialize every cell exactly (missing -> "", others -> str),          │
│                          │ factorize columns once into integer codes and value lengths, build three cheap candidate  │
│                          │ row-field orderings — (A) a global frequency-ranked column order using                    │
│                          │ sum(len(v)*cnt*(cnt-1)), (B) a recursive conditional prefix partition tree picking        │
│                          │ per-group columns by length-weighted pair repetition and permuting only within groups,    │
│                          │ and (C) a variant using immediate (cnt-1) savings — then score each candidate's           │
│                          │ serialized rows with the deterministic ideal Trie objective (sorted strings, adjacent LCP │
│                          │ via C-speed slice-equality binary search) and output the best. Every original cell value  │
│                          │ and row is preserved (values copied verbatim into object-dtype rows), each row gets a     │
│                          │ valid column-ordering list consistent with the returned data, `col_merge` reuses the      │
│                          │ parent `merging_columns` when available, and the public `reorder` signature is unchanged. │
