│                          │ that altered/dropped data and could crash. The fix replaces the algorithm with a correct, │
│                          │ bounded construction: serialize all cells once, build three candidate per-row column      │
│                          │ orderings — (1) a global order ranked by sum len(v)*count(v)*(count(v)-1), (2) an         │
│                          │ alternative len-weighted pair-repetition ranking, and (3) a recursive conditional         │
│                          │ partition tree that branches on the column with the largest length-weighted repeated-pair │
│                          │ savings inside each group — then score each candidate with the exact ideal character-Trie │
│                          │ reuse (sum of LCPs of lexicographically adjacent serialized rows, computed with C-speed   │
│                          │ slice comparisons and binary-search LCP), select the best, and emit a per-row permuted    │
│                          │ DataFrame (object dtype, all original values preserved) plus matching per-row column      │
│                          │ orderings. Column merges and one-way dependencies are honored as adjacency constraints in │
│                          │ each row's ordering. No extra columns, no dropped rows, no fabricated values.             │
