│ patch_description        │ Keep the prior architecture (one-time serialization + integer factorization, three        │
│                          │ bounded candidate constructions scored by the exact sorted-LCP Trie objective) and add    │
│                          │ the recommended bounded adjacent-swap hill-climb refinement: starting from the best flat  │
│                          │ global column order, repeatedly try swapping each adjacent column pair, accept a swap     │
│                          │ only when the exact Trie reuse score improves, capped at ~20 sweeps and a ~2.5s           │
│                          │ wall-clock budget. The refined order is scored against all candidates (including the      │
│                          │ conditional tree) and only kept if it truly wins under the real serial-Trie character     │
│                          │ objective. All scoring uses C-speed slice comparisons and shared serialized strings;      │
│                          │ per-row orders from the tree still compete, so the plateaued dataset gets a fresh search  │
│                          │ direction while the others are unchanged if no improvement is found.                      │
